  "doc": "Hush cutout rig (TECH 4.7). px at zoom 1.0, y down, faces +x; `_r` = near side. offset = child joint in the parent's joint frame (root: joint above the FEET ORIGIN); pivot/sockets = canvas px of the part texture (joint = pivot; socket [x, y, rot]); world = parent * T(offset + pose.xy) * R(rot) * S(sx, sy); pose root channels = a transform about the feet origin applied first. Limb bones (`draw: limb:<id>`) are invisible; each limb is a round-capped hose through its joints' world positions (quadratic, control = 2*mid - (a+b)/2), `width` fill + `outline` ink each side. Parts with `visible: false` are hidden unless a pose sets vis 1. Face slots: canvas `pivot` placed on head * T(face.offset); pupils shift within `range` and hide while eyes is one of `hide_with`. Skins swap textures by path (skins.<id>.files) and limb fills; pivots are identical.",
